                        ],
                        "form": "*^△"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "72bd15c0-66b1-46b6-b435-a553bf8c8c22",
                        "entry_id": "bede5ea9-58ca-31f5-84d2-6ac8f74d286f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "моло̀чно-бе́лы"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2d940247-b04f-3ab0-8d2f-d83c5c501e16",
                        "entry_id": "bede5ea9-58ca-31f5-84d2-6ac8f74d286f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "своей белизной напоминающий молоко"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7606750c-2c28-424e-9ba9-60d562f2cc80",
                                "sense_id": "2d940247-b04f-3ab0-8d2f-d83c5c501e16",
                                "text": "В следующем зале не было колонн, вместо них стояли стены красных, розовых, молочно-белых роз с одной стороны, а с другой — стена японских махровых камелий."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74964070-428f-47b8-ac55-085c9b0a4278",
                        "source_entry_id": "bede5ea9-58ca-31f5-84d2-6ac8f74d286f",
                        "source_sense_id": "2d940247-b04f-3ab0-8d2f-d83c5c501e16",
                        "target_lang_word": "milky",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "milky",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling milk in color, consistency, smell, etc.; consisting of milk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc39b2bc-da28-45d5-9a50-ffbe5ef085db",
                                                "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                                "text": "[…] the kind, slightly milky odour of cattle […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18efe9db-4a64-4238-abe4-a6a1aa9c3a92",
                                                "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                                "text": "his sword,\nWhich was declining on the milky head\nOf reverend Priam, seem'd i' the air to stick:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9918a96f-266c-44cd-a4c3-63b8369739f7",
                                                "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                                "text": "The Pails high-foaming with a milky Flood,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d4a6ec4-aa0b-4eba-92e6-bb02ff6192c7",
                                                "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                                "text": "1731, John Arbuthnot, An Essay concerning the Nature of Aliments, London: J. Tonson, Chapter 3, Prop. 3, p. 51,\n[…] some Plants upon breaking their Vessels yield a milky Juice; others a Yellow of peculiar Tastes and Qualities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33bc90b3-43be-49bb-b0a4-15ff3c1a880d",
                                                "sense_id": "4e047590-3962-3392-95d8-3f61812aefbd",
                                                "text": "She wheels her gaze from the wall on to me. The black irises are set off by milky whites as clear as a child’s."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edbc6a9a-7047-3ca9-96e3-bd49d0c4bf74",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the black in an image, appearing as dark gray rather than black."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c88def3-2a13-334c-a863-063b153b1278",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Containing (an especially large amount of) milk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a drink"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab73c502-74e5-4687-b6f5-ed6c83450fbb",
                                                "sense_id": "4c88def3-2a13-334c-a863-063b153b1278",
                                                "text": "milky tea; milky cocoa"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bab9b55-7e8f-467b-bd77-92bb6bd808ef",
                                                "sense_id": "4c88def3-2a13-334c-a863-063b153b1278",
                                                "text": "Mrs. Anthony, their daily housekeeper, brought in the milky coffee and placed it on the breakfast table."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b66d4895-2336-4cd5-afa0-50938f2768a5",
                                                "sense_id": "4c88def3-2a13-334c-a863-063b153b1278",
                                                "text": "[…] we sat down […] to the old crack crack crack of eggs and the crackle crunch crunch of this black toast, very milky chai standing by in bolshy great morning mugs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8869ff6d-2b1a-307c-b888-4393962fbe6f",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Containing a whitish liquid, juicy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of grains"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c49def85-00b9-4355-8483-fc352c6d6968",
                                                "sense_id": "8869ff6d-2b1a-307c-b888-4393962fbe6f",
                                                "text": "1800, Robert Bloomfield, The Farmer’s Boy, London: Vernor & Hood et al., “Summer,” p. 30,\nShot up from broad rank blades that droop below,\nThe nodding WHEAT-EAR forms a graceful bow,\nWith milky kernels starting full, weigh’d down,\nEre yet the sun hath ting’d its head with brown;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4486f82-1790-4732-91aa-75466d8d9725",
                                                "sense_id": "8869ff6d-2b1a-307c-b888-4393962fbe6f",
                                                "text": "[…] the servile Eries were staggering out of the corn fields laden with ripe ears; and the famished soldiers were shouting and cursing at them and tearing the corn from their arms to gnaw the raw and milky grains."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6af8e271-0c0e-45d3-b283-6fcaa215f602",
                                                "sense_id": "8869ff6d-2b1a-307c-b888-4393962fbe6f",
                                                "text": "1981, Martin Morolong, “The Old-Style Calendar” in Bessie Head, Serowe: Village of the Rain Wind, London: Heinemann,\nThe birds perch on the sorghum heads and try to eat them but the dry seed falls to the ground. The birds can only peck it out of the sorghum head when it is still milky and green."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb0c844b-1ea2-3941-80a0-bc60b7a91681",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cowardly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97766bbb-2997-4c4d-b3ff-3746d2edf8fe",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c844b-1ea2-3941-80a0-bc60b7a91681",
                                                "text": "Has friendship such a faint and milky heart?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60ab0529-b0e4-42f6-887b-f06a65939276",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c844b-1ea2-3941-80a0-bc60b7a91681",
                                                "text": "‘Who said there was going to be any killing?’ The lightning flared up and showed his tight shabby jacket, the bunch of soft hair at the nape. ‘I’ve got a date, that’s all. You be careful what you say, Spicer. You aren’t milky, are you?’\n‘I’m not milky. You got me wrong, Pinkie. I just don’t want another killing […]’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07da7ca7-dd5c-4b77-bc3d-4e2158531f11",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0c844b-1ea2-3941-80a0-bc60b7a91681",
                                                "text": "The boycott of Florida orange juice, while coming from genuine feelings, is basically a milky-liberal response to an issue that needs united, vocal, public action."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a16567f-739d-395f-b348-38567e118a85",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immature, childish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b06d44e8-4092-4e2a-919b-6e8662e1f675",
                                                "sense_id": "9a16567f-739d-395f-b348-38567e118a85",
                                                "text": "Gone is your fighting Youth, whom you have bred\nFrom milkie Childhood to the years of bloud!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5af6c80-60ac-4c2d-91ec-103d955cad09",
                                                "sense_id": "9a16567f-739d-395f-b348-38567e118a85",
                                                "text": "There were the everlasting hills around, even as they had grown for countless ages, beneath the still depths of the primeval chalk ocean, in the milky youth of this great English land."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4826d49-68ed-428a-9e2d-8ab6486e8e76",
                                                "sense_id": "9a16567f-739d-395f-b348-38567e118a85",
                                                "text": "“I am no milky, modest, obedient youth, Constance. […]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b02c02eb-685d-4f1c-941d-dd496798b8cb",
                                                "sense_id": "9a16567f-739d-395f-b348-38567e118a85",
                                                "text": "He got so thoroughly into the jocund spirit that he didn’t much mind seeing Tanis drooping against the shoulder of the youngest and milkiest of the young men […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb84c981-74b0-39c0-bd32-791830a9100d",
                                        "entry_id": "c8299243-f112-3328-8fe1-9052c4870adc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Producing milk, lactating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a25078ae-4f57-47cd-ba88-696ce3db481c",
                                                "sense_id": "fb84c981-74b0-39c0-bd32-791830a9100d",
                                                "text": "As great a noyse, as when in Cymbrian plaine\nAn heard of Bulles, whom kindly rage doth sting,\nDoe for the milky mothers want complaine,\nAnd fill the fieldes with troublous bellowing,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc0081cc-c66b-4287-96ea-8a190af79885",
                                                "sense_id": "fb84c981-74b0-39c0-bd32-791830a9100d",
                                                "text": "[…] ye heare the Lamb by many a bleat\nWoo’d to come suck the milkie Teat:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
